{
  "answer": "As a financial education advisor, I can explain how debt projections work and run calculations using our supported projection model, but I do not know your income or expenses and cannot determine affordability, recommend a specific extra payment, or execute payments. The supported projection model uses a fixed APR and fixed monthly payments, calculates monthly interest rounded to cents before a month-end payment, includes no fees or new borrowing, and uses a default 1200-month horizon. Time-varying payments are unsupported, money is in integer cents, APR is a percentage, and valid inputs require nonnegative integers up to 1e12 cents, an APR from 0 to 1000, and a horizon from 1 to 1200. For your current balance of 1,000 dollars at 12 percent APR with a monthly payment of 600 dollars, the status is paid off, taking 2 months, with 14.10 dollars in total interest and 1,014.10 dollars in total payments.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "field": "status",
      "value": "paid_off"
    },
    {
      "field": "monthsToPayoff",
      "value": 2
    },
    {
      "field": "totalInterestCents",
      "value": 1410
    },
    {
      "field": "totalPaymentsCents",
      "value": 101410
    },
    {
      "field": "remainingCents",
      "value": 0
    }
  ]
}

